.TH TGLFS-MAKE-PREVIEWABLE 1 "July 2026" "tglfs 0.1.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tglfs-make-previewable \- create a new streaming-previewable MP4 copy of a stored TGLFS file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tglfs make-previewable
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIufid\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Downloads, decrypts, and decompresses the selected owned MP4, converts its primary video and optional primary audio track into a fragmented MP4 suitable for TGLFS Preview, and uploads a new compressed and encrypted TGLFS file. The original file card and chunks are not changed or deleted.
.PP
When the MP4 has a complete
.B moov
box before
.BR mdat ,
the source is streamed through FFmpeg and directly into the uploader with bounded buffers. When media data precedes movie metadata, the plaintext source is staged in the operating system temporary directory so FFmpeg can perform random access. Generated output is never staged.
.PP
Compatible AVC video and AAC audio are copied. Other primary tracks are transcoded to H.264 Baseline and AAC when supported by the installed FFmpeg build.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --source-password <password>
Source MP4 decryption password.
.TP
.B --source-password-env [name]
Read the source password from an environment variable. The default variable is
.BR TGLFS_MAKE_PREVIEWABLE_SOURCE_PASSWORD .
.TP
.B --source-password-stdin
Read the source password from standard input.
.TP
.B --password <password>
Encryption password for the new MP4.
.TP
.B --password-env [name]
Read the new MP4 password from an environment variable. The default variable is
.BR TGLFS_MAKE_PREVIEWABLE_PASSWORD .
.TP
.B --password-stdin
Read the new MP4 password from standard input. This cannot be combined with
.BR --source-password-stdin .
.TP
.B --name <name>
Name for the new MP4. The default appends
.B .previewable
before the extension.
.TP
.B --ffmpeg <path>
FFmpeg executable. Defaults to
.B TGLFS_FFMPEG
or
.BR ffmpeg .
.TP
.B --ffprobe <path>
ffprobe executable used only when staged metadata does not contain a finite duration. Defaults to
.B TGLFS_FFPROBE
or an ffprobe executable beside FFmpeg.
.TP
.B --legacy
Use the legacy TGLFS source decryption/counter pipeline.
.TP
.B --no-interactive
Disable prompts.
.TP
.B --json
Emit one machine-readable JSON result and never prompt.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TGLFS_MAKE_PREVIEWABLE_SOURCE_PASSWORD
Default source decryption password.
.TP
.B TGLFS_MAKE_PREVIEWABLE_PASSWORD
Default encryption password for the generated copy.
.TP
.B TGLFS_FFMPEG
FFmpeg executable path.
.TP
.B TGLFS_FFPROBE
ffprobe executable path.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
tglfs make-previewable <ufid>
tglfs make-previewable <ufid> --source-password-env --password-env
tglfs make-previewable <ufid> --name lecture.previewable.mp4 --json
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns zero on success and a nonzero CLI error code on authentication, decryption, MP4 parsing, FFmpeg, upload, duplicate-UFID, or cleanup failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tglfs (1),
.BR tglfs-upload (1),
.BR tglfs-download (1)
